>> with nethack-as-it-exists, and some things in nethack that
>> annoy the hell out of me but "fixing" them would require
>> rebalancing the game and likely alienate some users, and
>> the sheer volume of content that would need to be repeated
>> is breathtaking.

Before I started NetHack-De four years ago this weren't the questions
I asked myself.

I just wanted to combine two of my interest, NetHack and linguistics,
and the questions I had to answer before starting were:
Is it possible at all and will I be able to finish it?

I didn't even think about how many would like to play a German
NetHack.

But it is cool to see that the (still unfinished) translation gets
downloaded 50 to 100 times a month. :-D

> I think I've decided where I'm going to go with it.  And it's 
> something of a "middle way."  I'll make something 'familiar' 
> to nethackers, with a lot of features nethackers will recognize 
> (pets, shops, amulet of Yendor, Rodney, Vlad's tower, Medusa, 
> Fort Ludios, much of the item and monster lists, etc) but I've 
> decided to treat it as a successor with its own identity, rather 
> than a reimplementation effort attempting to recreate nethack's 
> balance and game mechanics.  I'll not attempt to recreate 
> "The Same Game" in detail.  I'll treat questions of balance and 
> game mechanics as needing new answers, not as having answers that 
> need copied from nethack. 

Good luck!

> I'll skip things I think might be infringing.  I'll skip things 
> that don't belong with the things that are there (anachronistic, 
> Australian, Japanese, and Chinese elements should be in games 
> with different settings).

I think it is part of the appeal of NetHack that it tries to mix a lot
of references and different elements tongue in cheek.

NetHack doesn't take itself as serious as for example Angband does.

> I'll skip things that are too 
> arbitrary or obscure (ie, useful only to the spoiled and make 
> no sense anyway, like cursed scrolls of gold detection).  I'll 

Don't you mean reading confused scrolls of gold detection?

A cursed ?oGD shows all traps on the level as $ which IMO is a totally
acceptable behavior for a cursed scrolls.

Cursed scrolls should do something nasty.

> skip things that in my opinion give the player too many options 
> (like wishes).

If you completely eliminate wishes, do you provide an easy way to let
the player get those items he thinks he needs for an ascension?

It is rather annoying to wait several thousands turn to get an item
one really "needs".

> I'll fundamentally change some races/classes and 
> eliminate others.

That is something everybody trying to do improve or fork NetHack
should do. The difference between classes is still lacking.

For example I think tourists shouldn't be able to be stealthy.
Although a fumbling intrinsic for tourists would be to harsh. 
:)

> I'll add a lot of new and unfamiliar material, 
> including some directly contradictory to the setting and background 
> of nethack.

Cool.

> It'll be a different game. 

I'm looking forward to play it.

